# Meeting Notes 1

## Project: Payment Processing System

**Meeting Objective:**
Discuss the project requirements, define the scope of the Payment Processing System, identify the minimum viable product (MVP), and establish the overall architecture and implementation plan.

---

# Project Overview

The team will develop a **Payment Processing System** that simulates the complete lifecycle of financial payments. The application will expose REST APIs to create, process, validate, and track payments while maintaining a complete audit trail of every status transition.

The system is intended to demonstrate enterprise-level payment processing concepts without integrating with real payment gateways.

---

# Project Goals

The primary objectives discussed during the meeting are:

* Build a RESTful Payment Processing API.
* Simulate the complete payment lifecycle.
* Maintain complete payment history.
* Record every payment status transition.
* Design a scalable and maintainable architecture.
* Build a frontend application to interact with the APIs.
* Ensure the system can be easily extended with future enhancements.

---

# Payment Lifecycle

Every payment will follow a predefined workflow:

```text
CREATED
    │
    ▼
VALIDATED
    │
    ▼
SENT
    │
    ▼
COMPLETED
```

If an error occurs during any stage of processing, the payment will transition to:

```text
FAILED
```

---

# Payment Status Definitions

| Status        | Description                                                              |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **CREATED**   | Payment request has been received and stored.                            |
| **VALIDATED** | Payment has successfully passed all validation checks.                   |
| **SENT**      | Payment has been transmitted for processing.                             |
| **COMPLETED** | Payment has been processed successfully.                                 |
| **FAILED**    | Payment processing failed due to validation, business, or system errors. |

---

# Core Functional Requirements

The team agreed that the first implementation should include:

* Create a new payment.
* Retrieve payment details.
* Retrieve payment status.
* View complete payment history.
* Search payments by status.
* Display failure reasons for unsuccessful payments.

---

# Payment Validation Rules

Before processing a payment, the following validations will be performed:

* Required fields must be present.
* Payment amount must be greater than zero.
* Currency must be valid.
* Sender account must exist.
* Receiver account must exist.
* Sender account must have sufficient balance.

Payments failing any validation will immediately transition to the **FAILED** state.

---

# Audit Trail

One of the key project requirements is maintaining a complete audit history.

Every payment status change should record:

* Previous Status
* New Status
* Timestamp
* Triggered By (User/System)
* Error Code (if applicable)
* Failure Reason (if applicable)

This audit trail will support debugging, monitoring, and future compliance requirements.

---

# REST API Scope

The backend will expose REST endpoints for payment management, including:

* Create Payment
* Retrieve All Payments
* Retrieve Payment by ID
* Retrieve Payment History
* Update Payment Status
* Filter Payments by Status

The API will follow RESTful principles and return appropriate HTTP status codes.

